# Assignment 02 - Deep Reinforcement Learning

## Overview

This assignment explores Deep Reinforcement Learning techniques through two different applications:

1. Autonomous Drone Battery Management using DQN and Double DQN
2. Sepsis Treatment Optimization using Actor-Critic

---

## Problem 1: Autonomous Drone Battery Management using DQN and DDQN

The objective is to develop an autonomous drone surveillance environment with battery management and train reinforcement learning agents using:

- Deep Q-Network (DQN)
- Double Deep Q-Network (DDQN)

The environment considers:

- Drone position
- Battery level
- Charging stations
- Dynamic Points of Interest (POIs)
- Atmospheric disturbances
- Energy consumption

The performance of DQN and Double DQN is evaluated and compared using training and evaluation rewards.

### Techniques Used

- Deep Q-Network (DQN)
- Double DQN (DDQN)
- Experience Replay
- Target Network
- Epsilon-Greedy Exploration
- TensorFlow/Keras

---

## Problem 2: Sepsis Treatment Optimization using Actor-Critic

The objective is to model ICU treatment as a Reinforcement Learning environment and train an Actor-Critic agent to suggest medical interventions based on patient information.

### State Features

- Mean Blood Pressure (mean_bp)
- Oxygen Saturation (spo2)
- Respiratory Rate (resp_rate)
- Age
- Gender

The environment contains 99 possible medical intervention actions.

### Techniques Used

- Actor-Critic Reinforcement Learning
- Actor Network
- Critic Network
- Reward-based policy learning
- TensorFlow/Keras
- Clinical data preprocessing

The reward function is based on the deviation of patient vital signs from defined target values.

